1) Code a method named eye that takes as input a positive integer d and prints out an identity
matrix of size (d x d). An identity matrix is defined as a matrix with 1s on the diagonal and 0s
everywhere else. For example, if the user enters 3, your program should print out:
1 0 0
0 1 0
0 0 1
The method does not return anything. Hint: Use nested loops!
2) Code a method named findMyString that takes two input variables, arr and key. Assume that
the key is only a single String and that arr is an array of Strings of any length. Your method
should search for key in arr and returns the first position (index) of its appearance in the array.
In the case the key is not found, your output should be -1.
For example:
For arr:
Hello Hey Dog Apple Restaurant Red Stove
For key: Dog – your output should be 2.
For key: Red – your output should be 5.
For key: Cat – your output should be -1.
3) Code a method named addArray that returns an array of int and has two parameters of type
array of int, called arr1 and arr2. The method should add up corresponding elements of arr1 and
arr2 and return their result.
4) Extra practice: Repeat question 3, however, make it work with arrays of unequal length. When
adding to the smaller array, you can assume the missing elements are zero.
For arr1 => {1, 2, 3, 4} and arr2 => {1,2,3} – your output should be {2, 4, 6, 4}
Make sure to test all your methods in your main appropriately.